What is digital HIRARC with AI?
Digital HIRARC uses software to manage Hazard Identification, Risk Assessment and Risk Control. AI can help surface recurring hazards and patterns in safety records, while people validate findings and decide controls. NeoEHS connects these activities with inspections, incidents, corrective actions and permit workflows to support ongoing risk management.

The real test of HIRARC happens after approval
A risk assessment may be complete, signed and neatly filed. Then a delivery route changes, a machine guard is removed for maintenance, or a contractor starts work beside an operating production line.

The document has not changed. The exposure has.

For an HSE manager, the difficult question is often not whether a HIRARC exists. It is whether the assessment still describes the work being done today—and whether the controls listed in it actually work.

