Frequently asked questions
What is digital HIRARC?
Digital HIRARC uses software to record hazards, assess risks, assign controls and maintain review records. Its value is connecting the assessment to the people, actions and evidence needed to manage workplace exposure.

How can AI support HIRARC?
AI can help identify related reports and recurring patterns in safety data. Its findings need review against the original records and actual work conditions before they influence an approved assessment.

Can NeoEHS support HIRARC in Malaysia?
NeoEHS publishes support for configurable risk assessment and HIRARC alongside related safety workflows. Organisations should confirm the required matrix, approvals, integrations and evidence requirements during implementation.

Can AI approve a risk assessment on its own?
AI should support the assessment team. Responsible people should validate hazards, decide appropriate controls and approve the assessment under the organisation’s procedures.

How is a HIRARC risk score calculated?
The example method in Malaysia’s DOSH HIRARC Guidelines uses likelihood multiplied by severity. The organisation should apply defined rating criteria consistently and retain the reasoning behind each rating.

When should a digital HIRARC be reviewed?
Set planned reviews and additional triggers for changed work, incidents, new findings or evidence that controls are ineffective. The review should consider the task as it is currently performed.

Does HIRARC software guarantee legal compliance?
No. Software supports documentation and follow-up. Applicable duties still require suitable assessment, implementation of necessary controls and appropriate workplace management by the responsible parties.

Is HIRARC the same as a permit to work?
No. HIRARC identifies hazards, evaluates risk and determines controls. A permit to work authorises specified work under defined conditions. The two processes should inform each other where relevant.
